people of the internet's retroreckon  tour here and in today's video we'll be  talking about how  i would keep the hype alive for hogwarts  legacy because right now  i gotta be honest guys it feels like it  could be  dying a little bit of course we didn't  get any news at this year's e3 or the  summer game fest and i admit it's easy  for us as youtubers and fans to sit back  and critique what should have been done  or what might have been done but it's  not always so  simple on the other side today i want to  put my money where my mouth is so to  speak and actually try  and think through what the best  marketing tactics would be for a big  game like this  should they be saying anything at all  right now should they be quiet right now  should they be  doing an all-out marketing blitz we're  gonna talk about all of that here  today okay so part one here marketing  background i do have a little bit of  experience in  marketing and communications with a  major company and also have a graduate  degree  in the field now it's not what i work on  now and i don't want you to think i have  some huge  extensive background but i have studied  it and know a little bit about it here  now first off here one thing i can tell  you is that the marketing team is almost  certainly completely separate from those  who are actually working on the game  you see there's this common critique  that i see among fans whenever you have  one fan who's saying man i really want  to see more a screenshot or  a new trailer or i want to see gameplay  whatever it may be a very popular retort  that i see to that is that another fan  will come in and say  guys you're crazy we can't rush  avalanche what are you doing we don't  want another cyberpunk  seriously if i have to see that one more  time i might scream  well i agree we should not rush the  development those comments don't quite  make sense in this context  as i mentioned the folks in charge of  promoting this game probably don't work  on the game itself instead you have your  advertising agencies you have pr  firms and wb as the publisher for the  game almost certainly has some folks in  these roles within their own company  avalanche probably even has folks who  work on these tasks  specifically as well but these are not  your game designers or coders or writers  we're in a completely different area  here so if we're talking about  getting a few screenshots tweeting out  information advertising that sort of  thing it's not going to be taking away  time from game development except for  one  little issue that we'll talk about here  in a bit but for the most part this is  completely separate so you guys don't  have to worry whenever someone says they  want to see more of the game that  doesn't mean they want avalanche to rush  and put it out tomorrow it  just means we want to see more that's it  now how these things will usually work  is the folks in charge at wb will set up  a  marketing plan for the game they'll  decide how much money they're going to  put into promoting the title and then  they'll task the marketing team with  going out and making it happen  the folks in marketing will have regular  meetings and conversations with those  actually making the game to get an idea  of their progress and also  of course so they know what's in the  game after all if they're going to mark  the title they'll need to know how it  plays the overall story  etc plus those folks on the inside will  have extensive access to research and  demographics about both the game the  target audience  things that i don't necessarily have  here so their marketing campaign should  end up being a lot better and more  targeted than what i'm able to put  together here  pressures on wb so in order to begin the  marketing campaign for  a game it's a good idea to know the  release date so we can kind of work  backward at least have a fairly narrow  release window  given that all we have right now is 2022  let's just  assume for the sake of our video here  today that hogwarts legacy will be  releasing around  july 2022 which would put it in the same  month as fantastic beasts three hitting  theaters  with that target month in mind that  gives us a full year of time for a  steady ramp up marketing campaign  and i think for a game this size roughly  a full year of steady planned out  promotion and tactics would be  ideal so for phase one of that plan i  would immediately start getting  more active on social media particularly  twitter and instagram  these could start out as weekly posts of  varying types some weeks maybe a new  screenshot or two other weeks may be a  random fact about the game and we could  even throw in polls here and there as  well  the challenge here is you obviously  don't want to bombard people with a  bunch of irrelevant tweets that no one  cares about but you do want to keep the  interest high and provide a steady  trickle of quality information and this  doesn't necessarily have to be  every single week for the next year but  i think some sort of consistent social  media presence would go a long way  toward keeping fans  engaged and excited and on the marketing  side of things it's completely  free there's literally no charge other  than what you're paying the marketing or  pr person to do this  it would only take a little bit of time  each week for someone to prepare and  send out the posts  even if you need to hit up the devs for  some screenshots that's something that's  not going to take a lot of time for them  to do  so if we start getting more active on  social media in july 2021  i would be sure to release a steady  stream of new screenshots throughout the  months of august and september maybe  showing off various creatures that we'll  encounter or even some locations that we  may visit  now with halloween being such a big  moment throughout the harry potter  series i think  october would be a unique opportunity to  reveal a little bit more about the  character creator and how it will work  in the game  considering this will almost certainly  happen at the opening of the game i  don't think anyone would be too worried  about having something like this  spoiled in fact it might be nice to get  an idea of how many options we'll have  and what the creator will be like so we  can start planning who we want to be  when the game releases  are we going to have beard options  avalanche i really need some strong  beard options in this game  when november hits this is our time to  really start teasing that full  gameplay reveal i'd ratchet up the  social media posts here and maybe even  have some sort of interactive scavenger  hunt or game for fans to figure out the  release date for the long time old  school harry potter fans you guys  remember how much we obsessed over jk  rowling's website the door  how could anyone forget that door and  now she actually revealed the title for  deathly hallows through that little  online game among  other things that she revealed to the  site if there's one thing you know for  sure about harry potter fans it's that  we love digging for clues and trying to  solve riddles and puzzles  december would put us at about seven  months out and considering this is also  the month for the game awards i think it  makes perfect sense to finally show a  brand new trailer here  with a specific focus on gameplay  ideally this would also be a great time  to announce the release date you could  possibly follow this up with another  playstation blog post similar to what  they did after the initial reveal  trailer now when it comes to the trailer  this is the point that would require  some work  on the side of the developers at  avalanche so in the opening we talked  about how  this is completely separate here we've  got our pr guys we've got our marketing  guys  they're focused on the promotion of the  game however to build something like  a trailer at that point you are going to  need some of those cinematics folks from  over at avalanche to help  create that trailer so at this point you  can make a pretty strong  argument that this would actually pull  people from working on the game to  create this trailer i think it's worth  it i think they have to have  another trailer i've actually heard  horror stories about devs prepping for  big trailers for e3 when they have  almost nothing ready to show  so this is the point where i hear you  when you say don't rush avalanche of  course you want to make sure that they  have ample time to work on their other  tasks but i think you also have to  consider the importance of  marketing and making a good trailer to  make sure this game gets  out to the public and so more people see  this from here we would ride the wave  of momentum from the trailer throughout  january and into the month of february  all while continuing our active presence  on social media  once we get into march we're now only  four months away  and this is the point i would look to  reveal a hogwarts legacy collector's  edition  i already made a separate video which  i'll link to in the card above about  specifically what i would like to see  as part of a hogwarts legacy collector's  edition and even if it doesn't have the  items i want i definitely think it would  be a  huge missed opportunity for this game  not to have some sort of special edition  with a few goodies in store for us die  hard fans for the month of april 2022  i'd try and get some sort of deep dive  interview with one of the developers of  the game and start doing more interviews  with various video game news sites and  youtube influencers  hey if anyone at avalanche or wb wants  to chat a bit feel free to reach out  just a few questions not too many that's  all i promise  as for the month of may i'd really try  and hone in on some cross promotion with  fantastic beasts 3.  this could be in the form of a special  tv advertisement that focuses on both  setting up plans to show the hogwarts  legacy trailer in the movie theater for  folks watching the movie  and maybe even throwing in a free  fantastic beasts movie ticket for anyone  who pre-orders the game  i think little things like that would go  a long way and it's a great opportunity  to cross promote between the two  properties  once june hits we're almost there and  this is when i'd really  ramp up on the online advertisements  both in the form of youtube and twitch  ads  as well as display and web banner ads on  some of the most popular harry potter  sites as well as video game sites and  that would take us  all the way up to the month of july  which in this fun little mock example  we're doing is the pretend release date  for the game woohoo  we finally made it guys if you all enjoy  this marketing plan hit that thumbs  up button before you go let wb know hey  i'd like to see something like this and  if not let me know down in the comments  what you would like to see instead  as always thank you all so much for  watching i'll talk to you again soon

